/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The use of ECG, or also known as Electrocardiograms, can represent the electrical behaviour of the heart and in parallel, are employed as diagnostic tools for detecting arrhythmias, unsystematic variations of the cardiac pulsations.)
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [1]
>>
