/E (Due to the high beat density in many ECG recordings, the article [5] reported that retaining at least three consecutive beats preserves arrhythmia morphologies and optimizes information retention, while enhancing model generalization and noise suppression. Accordingly, [6] a 2.3 second sliding window enables capturing three full cycles under low-frequency conditions.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [2]
